# Zoho: no app branding

Never send this app’s name, product name, or internal branding into Zoho (Inventory, Books, or any Zoho API).

## Forbidden in Zoho-bound fields

Do not put any of these (or close variants) in `notes`, `description`, `memo`, `reference_number`, line descriptions, journal narration, User-Agent, or any other Zoho payload/header:

- `HR & BI`, `HR&BI`, `HR and BI`
- `hr-attendance`, `hr-attendance-app`, `hr-attendance-backend`
- `Purchase Planning` as a product/app label (plan numbers like `PP-…` in references are fine)
- Phrases like “Generated from … app”, “Review completed by admin before sending”

## Required behavior

- Leave Zoho `notes` empty / omit them unless the user explicitly supplies business text for Zoho.
- Use a neutral User-Agent (e.g. `lifesmile-zoho-client`), never app-repo names.
- Operational IDs (PO numbers, settlement IDs, batch `#123`) are OK when they do not name this app.
- Internal comments and UI copy may mention the module; Zoho-facing strings must not.

```js
// ❌ BAD — visible in Zoho Notes
notes: `Generated from HR & BI Purchase Planning plan ${plan.planNumber}. …`

// ✅ GOOD — omit notes, or only vendor/business text the user asked for
const payload = { vendor_id, purchaseorder_number, date, reference_number, line_items }
```
